# ✅ Zuri Production Deployment Checklist

This file tracks all final changes needed before moving the app to production.

---

## 🔐 Security
- [ ] Remove or rotate all test accounts
- [ ] Use environment-specific `.env.production` with secure secrets
- [ ] Enable HTTPS on the frontend domain
- [ ] Add CSRF protection if sessions remain server-side

## 📧 Email Setup
- [x] Configure Gmail App Passwords
- [x] Test reset-password email link delivery
- [ ] Set up email logs to monitor bounce/failure rates

## 🔒 Password Reset Flow
- [x] Token stored securely in DB
- [x] Token expires after 30 minutes
- [ ] Implement `/reset-password/confirm` to update user password
- [ ] Invalidate token after use
- [ ] Log resets for audit trail

## 🛠️ Backend
- [x] Confirm all routes require appropriate `requireLogin` or `requireAdmin`
- [ ] Enable error logging with timestamps (optional: Winston or Pino)
- [ ] Move sensitive constants to `.env`

## 🧪 Testing
- [ ] Test login/logout on production server
- [ ] Test expired tokens
- [ ] Test invalid username flow
- [ ] Test without internet / network failure

## 🌍 Deployment
- [ ] Set `NODE_ENV=production`
- [ ] Compress/minify frontend build
- [ ] Ensure all static assets are served properly
- [ ] Monitor PostgreSQL errors (pg logs)

## 🧹 Final Cleanup
- [ ] Remove console logs (or wrap in `if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production')`)
- [ ] Confirm favicon and manifest are correct
- [ ] Confirm mobile responsiveness
- [ ] Verify headers and footers match brand

